(6548472, 974137, 125275, '<td valign="top">Nice colors and interesting idea.</td>', 'Nice colors and interesting idea.', '2011-09-22 21:24:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548473, 974120, 125275, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your blue! I''m going to guess <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=59267" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">william88</a> and I hope you include at least a hint of how this was done. (Jello?)<br/> <br/>So is the whole contraption on some sort of movable table that is quickly lowered from underneath? The wine glasses seem to be fixed with some sort of adhesive at their bases. It could go down, then a fraction of a second later the picture is snapped - before the liquid splashes down.</td>', 'Congrats on your blue! I''m going to guess  william88 and I hope you include at least a hint of how this was done. (Jello?) So is the whole contraption on some sort of movable table that is quickly lowered from underneath? The wine glasses seem to be fixed with some sort of adhesive at their bases. It could go down, then a fraction of a second later the picture is snapped - before the liquid splashes down.', '2011-09-22 21:29:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548489, 973905, 125275, '<td valign="top">I will have to come back and check, but I think I recognize those candles and the table from another entry in the "above" challenge...so going on a limb again...<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=136704" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">pederlol</a>?<br/> <br/>Interesting tones in this one. Seems to have a cool temperature. The hand seems to also cast a morose tone to the image; the nails are an unhealthy looking color in this light! Interesting idea; I''m curious to see where it will finish.</td>', 'I will have to come back and check, but I think I recognize those candles and the table from another entry in the "above" challenge...so going on a limb again... pederlol? Interesting tones in this one. Seems to have a cool temperature. The hand seems to also cast a morose tone to the image; the nails are an unhealthy looking color in this light! Interesting idea; I''m curious to see where it will finish.', '2011-09-22 21:43:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548508, 973778, 47470, '<td valign="top">This is over-sharpened for my taste.  The green also looks sickly, which doesn''t fit with a subject that is usually considered high-class.  I think the green could have worked if either the title pulled it together or if the green was a more lush, dark shade.</td>', 'This is over-sharpened for my taste.  The green also looks sickly, which doesn''t fit with a subject that is usually considered high-class.  I think the green could have worked if either the title pulled it together or if the green was a more lush, dark shade.', '2011-09-22 22:51:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548512, 973705, 47470, '<td valign="top">The processing seems to have darkened the wine and brought out more detail, which, to me, makes it look thick, like chocolate!  With such a clean background, I would have preferred a dainty female hand.  I think the male hand would have worked better with a restaurant scene in the background to make it look like a fancy waiter was pouring the drink.  I lover the texture of the liquid inside the glass.</td>', 'The processing seems to have darkened the wine and brought out more detail, which, to me, makes it look thick, like chocolate!  With such a clean background, I would have preferred a dainty female hand.  I think the male hand would have worked better with a restaurant scene in the background to make it look like a fancy waiter was pouring the drink.  I lover the texture of the liquid inside the glass.', '2011-09-22 22:53:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548513, 974011, 47470, '<td valign="top">I love this idea.  I wish the lighting was a bit moodier, maybe lit from just one side instead of both sides.</td>', 'I love this idea.  I wish the lighting was a bit moodier, maybe lit from just one side instead of both sides.', '2011-09-22 22:54:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548515, 973985, 47470, '<td valign="top">The lighting on the bottle is exquisitely silky.  Nice set-up.</td>', 'The lighting on the bottle is exquisitely silky.  Nice set-up.', '2011-09-22 22:55:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548518, 973999, 47470, '<td valign="top">I would have preferred a slightly longer lens so that the barrel would be comparatively larger in the frame.  I think all the action is in the second room, so the longer lens could have also trimmed down on the first room.  The second room looks so cozy!</td>', 'I would have preferred a slightly longer lens so that the barrel would be comparatively larger in the frame.  I think all the action is in the second room, so the longer lens could have also trimmed down on the first room.  The second room looks so cozy!', '2011-09-22 22:57:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548521, 973759, 47470, '<td valign="top">The lighting on the bottle is very well-executed!  The color adds a surprising and welcome change.  I love the texture in the bar too.  I can''t help but wish there was a slim female hand with a fat diamond ring on it resting on the bar as if a high-class lady was flirting with a tuxedo''d man just outside the frame.</td>', 'The lighting on the bottle is very well-executed!  The color adds a surprising and welcome change.  I love the texture in the bar too.  I can''t help but wish there was a slim female hand with a fat diamond ring on it resting on the bar as if a high-class lady was flirting with a tuxedo''d man just outside the frame.', '2011-09-22 22:59:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548523, 974088, 47470, '<td valign="top">I''m all for moody lighting, but I wish that at least the highlights were a bit brighter to add a touch more contrast.</td>', 'I''m all for moody lighting, but I wish that at least the highlights were a bit brighter to add a touch more contrast.', '2011-09-22 23:01:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548524, 973632, 47470, '<td valign="top">Now THAT is how you do moody lighting.  The amount of separation between the subjects and background is perfect.</td>', 'Now THAT is how you do moody lighting.  The amount of separation between the subjects and background is perfect.', '2011-09-22 23:04:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548525, 973770, 47470, '<td valign="top">I love the colors and the soft texture of the background.  It has a great subtly exotic feel.  Wonderful vignette too.</td>', 'I love the colors and the soft texture of the background.  It has a great subtly exotic feel.  Wonderful vignette too.', '2011-09-22 23:06:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548527, 974151, 47470, '<td valign="top">I love the blur at the top and the bottom.</td>', 'I love the blur at the top and the bottom.', '2011-09-22 23:07:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548529, 973677, 47470, '<td valign="top">I love the texture inside the wine glasses.  BnW was a perfect choice for this.</td>', 'I love the texture inside the wine glasses.  BnW was a perfect choice for this.', '2011-09-22 23:08:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548531, 974022, 47470, '<td valign="top">I don''t think the tilt adds much for me.  It seems a bit extreme, like the bottle is going to fall out of the frame any second.  I love the light on the background though.</td>', 'I don''t think the tilt adds much for me.  It seems a bit extreme, like the bottle is going to fall out of the frame any second.  I love the light on the background though.', '2011-09-22 23:10:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548532, 973848, 47470, '<td valign="top">I appreciate the geometry in this, but I wish there was a touch more light on the bottle and glasses.</td>', 'I appreciate the geometry in this, but I wish there was a touch more light on the bottle and glasses.', '2011-09-22 23:10:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548533, 973957, 47470, '<td valign="top">I love the story that the title adds to this.  The colors and the background also add a lovely country atmosphere that I really enjoy.  Great use of negative space too.</td>', 'I love the story that the title adds to this.  The colors and the background also add a lovely country atmosphere that I really enjoy.  Great use of negative space too.', '2011-09-22 23:12:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548538, 973841, 47470, '<td valign="top">Nice set-up, but I think you tried to pull out too much texture, especially in the glass.  It makes the glasses and the bottles look dirty.  I love that the marble is broken--unexpected throw-back to ancient Greece, which is what still lifes with wine always make me think of : )<br/> <br/>On an unrelated note, I''m guessing this was taken by an American because of the color of that cheese.  Cheddar with wine makes me want to cry : )</td>', 'Nice set-up, but I think you tried to pull out too much texture, especially in the glass.  It makes the glasses and the bottles look dirty.  I love that the marble is broken--unexpected throw-back to ancient Greece, which is what still lifes with wine always make me think of : ) On an unrelated note, I''m guessing this was taken by an American because of the color of that cheese.  Cheddar with wine makes me want to cry : )', '2011-09-22 23:15:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548540, 973870, 47470, '<td valign="top">I love the lipstick stain.  I wish the glasses were a bit sharper, at least on their edges.</td>', 'I love the lipstick stain.  I wish the glasses were a bit sharper, at least on their edges.', '2011-09-22 23:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548566, 973958, 47470, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous location.  I think I would have cropped out just a little of the foreground stones.</td>', 'Gorgeous location.  I think I would have cropped out just a little of the foreground stones.', '2011-09-22 23:20:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548579, 974119, 47470, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Quite a capture!  Either you shot in burst mode or you have an enviously precise shutter finger : )  The detail of the cork hitting the glass is awesome.  Did the glass survive?</td>', 'Wow!  Quite a capture!  Either you shot in burst mode or you have an enviously precise shutter finger : )  The detail of the cork hitting the glass is awesome.  Did the glass survive?', '2011-09-22 23:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548604, 974006, 47470, '<td valign="top">Certo.<br/> <br/>The lighting leaves me wanting something, but I can''t decide if I want it a bit moodier or a bit Jill-Greenberg-esque.  I think a pair of laughing people would have gone so nicely with the sign.</td>', 'Certo. The lighting leaves me wanting something, but I can''t decide if I want it a bit moodier or a bit Jill-Greenberg-esque.  I think a pair of laughing people would have gone so nicely with the sign.', '2011-09-22 23:45:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548649, 973956, 47470, '<td valign="top">I really like the processing on this.</td>', 'I really like the processing on this.', '2011-09-23 00:28:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548650, 974095, 47470, '<td valign="top">My only nit-pick is that I wish you had showed the front label on the wine bottle instead of the back.  The back one probably isn''t as pretty.  Cool idea.  I love that you put wine in the vase.</td>', 'My only nit-pick is that I wish you had showed the front label on the wine bottle instead of the back.  The back one probably isn''t as pretty.  Cool idea.  I love that you put wine in the vase.', '2011-09-23 00:29:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6548898, 974069, 108069, '<td valign="top">Nice idea and really nice composition, but this seems to have some exposure and contrast issues that don''t really add to the photo in my opinion. I think some local contrast in the grass and stakes/vines in the foreground would add a sense of depth here, which is already apparent but could really be used to much better advantage, and should, as it''s a great aspect of this photo.<br/> <br/>That said, the sky actually looks over-contrasty and over-processed, and not to very good effect. (The hills look great, though).<br/> <br/>If I were to take a stab at editing this (WARNING: I over-edit and ruin everything) I''d start with some recovery adjustments in RAW, trying to recover some of the blown highlights in the clouds. Maybe a shadows/highlights adjustment in whatever else you use, and definitely a levels adjustment to bring up the blacks and mids and get a wider tonal range in the image.<br/> <br/>Then curves and/or sharpen mask tricks to boost local contrast to get a bit of pop. Maybe a bit of burn on the burnt-out grass to add texture.<br/> <br/>Composition-wise I really like it, though it looks like there''s a really nice white fence off to the right that could have been included more to provide a nice leading line and provide a bit of a natural frame to the photo.<br/> <br/>All the ingredients are here for an awesome image, and with a few tweaks it would be on another level.<br/> <br/>I hope you don''t mind the critique and me rambling on. I pointed out the technical things I''d work on personally as it''s a landscape, which to be honest aren''t typically loaded with emotion or personal attachment, and therefore the technical delivery matters more. Not voting, just rambling.</td>', 'Nice idea and really nice composition, but this seems to have some exposure and contrast issues that don''t really add to the photo in my opinion. I think some local contrast in the grass and stakes/vines in the foreground would add a sense of depth here, which is already apparent but could really be used to much better advantage, and should, as it''s a great aspect of this photo. That said, the sky actually looks over-contrasty and over-processed, and not to very good effect. (The hills look great, though). If I were to take a stab at editing this (WARNING: I over-edit and ruin everything) I''d start with some recovery adjustments in RAW, trying to recover some of the blown highlights in the clouds. Maybe a shadows/highlights adjustment in whatever else you use, and definitely a levels adjustment to bring up the blacks and mids and get a wider tonal range in the image. Then curves and/or sharpen mask tricks to boost local contrast to get a bit of pop. Maybe a bit of burn on the burnt-out grass to add texture. Composition-wise I really like it, though it looks like there''s a really nice white fence off to the right that could have been included more to provide a nice leading line and provide a bit of a natural frame to the photo. All the ingredients are here for an awesome image, and with a few tweaks it would be on another level. I hope you don''t mind the critique and me rambling on. I pointed out the technical things I''d work on personally as it''s a landscape, which to be honest aren''t typically loaded with emotion or personal attachment, and therefore the technical delivery matters more. Not voting, just rambling.', '2011-09-23 09:08:46.000000', NULL, 1),
